# The build context is everything in this directory, and Docker sends all of
# it to the daemon before the first instruction runs. Without this file that
# is the whole monorepo including every node_modules, which is hundreds of
# megabytes and takes minutes.
#
# The Dockerfile installs dependencies itself from the lockfile, so sending
# them is worse than pointless: a host's node_modules can contain binaries
# built for the wrong platform.
node_modules
**/node_modules

# Build output, which the image rebuilds.
dist
**/dist
**/.next
**/.astro
**/storybook-static

# Nothing here belongs in an image.
.git
.github
**/coverage
**/playwright-report
**/test-results
**/*.tsbuildinfo
.history
**/.env
**/.env.*
PLAN.md
